# data_shadows.syms — external DATA-constant symbols forced to header-less
# OBJECT shadows by abigen (--data-shadow-file). These are NSString/CF object
# constants exported by NATIVE x86_64 frameworks (an app's bundled PRIVATE
# frameworks like RedRock/iLifePageLayout, plus ObjC system frameworks not in
# ABICONV_SYM_SOURCES e.g. QTKit/ImageIO/DiscRecording/AddressBook). A
# translated i386 binary reads them with a 32-bit `movl slot(%rip),%reg`, which
# truncates the real >4GB symbol address and faults on the following deref.
# Header-typed NS/CF constants get shadows via the consider set; these have no
# headers, so they are listed explicitly. The shadow is a low-4GB var holding
# an objc handle wrapping the real object (x64_init_data_shadows + dlsym);
# static-interpose redirects the bind to it.
#
# GENERIC: regenerate/extend for any app with
#   src/86x64/_extract_data_shadows.sh <app.dylib> <libabiconv.dylib>
# and union the output here. It emits a binary's un-shadowed NATIVE-framework
# data constants read via a truncating 32-bit movl. dlsym-miss is a no-op, so
# unrelated apps that don't import a symbol are unaffected. Seeded from iPhoto
# (iLife '11); union of two extractor passes (the second after the first batch
# was applied, catching cases the load+deref must not be adjacent).
